  "visualBrief": "Individual Baitul Futuh compound: retained long stepped envelope,contemporary northern street frontage with a pale grand frame,original coarse gold screen around a broad round arch,vertical pale ribs and recessed opaque glazing,arched flanking fields and ground arcades;lower connecting blocks;southern angular prayer hall with tall rectangular glazing,round ground bays,grey stone panels,a silver ribbed dome and two glazed roof turrets;one small cupola over the front wing. Historic inscriptions,exact decorative motifs,garden,fencing,parked cars,neighboring buildings,furnished interiors and engineering are excluded.",
